The budget you reference as "responsible" was fueled primarily by tax cuts and the original projection was about half of what the actual deficit was and it was the right thing to do. The painful part is that I have to argue against my own position because every time anyone supporting this type of archaic fiscal policy pops up on social media they are either disingenuous, cherry pick their points, or don't care about contradictions so long as their team is the one committing the contradictions.
How much debt should Canada have?
